# Implementation Walkthrough - Phase 2: Attendance, Schedules, and Google Drive Sync

We have completed the second phase of changes, aligning the administration panels, schedules, batch date management, and Google Drive sync capabilities. Both codebases have been compile-verified and are fully wired.

## Key Enhancements

### 1. Two-Way Google Drive Deletion Sync & Direct Upload
- **Google Drive Storage Integration:** 
  - Notes uploaded in the Batch Management page are uploaded directly to Google Drive in the folder: `Root ➔ [Batch Name] ➔ Notes ➔ [Subject Name] ➔ [Filename.pdf]`.
  - Homework assignments uploaded in Batch Management are similarly uploaded directly to Google Drive in: `Root ➔ [Batch Name] ➔ Homework ➔ [Subject Name] ➔ [Filename.pdf]`.
  - Stored files carry their Google Drive file ID as `publicId` and use Drive preview links as their URLs, providing a unified storage scheme.
- **Two-way Sync & Automatic Background Sync:**
  - When notes or homework list endpoints are loaded in the dashboard sidebar, the backend triggers an asynchronous, non-blocking Google Drive sync (throttled to a 2-minute cooldown to prevent API overload). This automatically imports any new files teachers drag into Google Drive and cleans up DB records for files deleted from Google Drive.
  - Deleting a Google Drive synced note or homework in the UI calls the Google Drive API to instantly delete the file from the Google Drive storage.

### 2. Admin & Instructor Attendance Dashboard
- **Role Routing:** Modifying the main Attendance page (`frontend/src/app/dashboard/attendance/page.tsx`) routes students to their personal metrics page and admins/instructors to the Admin Attendance view.
- **Batch Rosters Panel:**
  - Displays quick-glance active batch metrics and overall attendance radial snapshots.
  - Includes a "Mark New Attendance" sheet where instructors can select a subject, date, and toggle students as Present/Absent with a single submission.
  - Provides a searchable Attendance Register log list where records can be filtered, edited (toggled Present/Absent), or deleted.
- **Student Profiles Panel:**
  - Side panel search to inspect any student's individual attendance, metrics breakdown per subject, and complete logs history (with inline edit/delete overrides).

### 3. Weekly Planner & Batch Future Schedules
- **Schedule page event creator:** The general Schedule page has been upgraded for Admins and Instructors. They now see a sidebar creator allowing them to schedule Classes, Exams, Assignments, Holidays, or Special lectures mapped to a Batch (offline), Course (online), or General campus-wide audience.
- **Future Scheduling & Recurrence:** In Batch Management, the class timing creator now includes a starting Date picker and Frequency selector (Weekly Recurring vs. One-Time). Weekly recurring classes automatically compute their recurrence weekday based on the selected date (e.g. scheduling on a Monday sets a weekly Monday recurring lecture).

