## Storage Layer Responsibilities (Neon DB vs Cloudinary vs Google Drive)

Here is a breakdown of how the three storage entities cooperate:

| Feature / Data Type | Neon PostgreSQL (learndb) | Cloudinary | Google Drive |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Relational Data & Metadata** | **Primary Store** (All schemas, Users, Batches, Courses, Attendance sheets, Schedules, and file metadata). | *None* | *None* |
| **Batch Notes & Homework PDFs** | Holds file URL, Google Drive file ID (`publicId`), and parsed text for AI search. | *Backup Fallback* (used only if Google Drive credentials are empty at startup). | **Primary Store** (Dynamic, nested folder hierarchy). |
| **Student Homework Submissions** | Stores references, grades, and review text. | **Primary Store** (Assigned files and student upload pdfs). | *None* (Kept separate to prevent cluttering official folders). |
| **Course Lesson Video / Images** | Video URLs, descriptions, lessons metadata. | **Primary Store** (Thumbnails, templates, rich media assets). | *None* |
| **Two-way Sync & Traversal** | Acts as the query target for UI feeds. | *None* | **Source of Truth** (Local filesystem representation for notes). |
